From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: BERBERIS_LOG_SYSCALLS / berberis.log_syscalls.<package>=1 logs the guest's syscalls (allow-list) to stderr

What the guest asks the kernel for: paths of open/stat/readlink/access/exec/unlink/mkdir, ptrace, prctl, rt_sigaction (new handler and flags), sockets, connect
(address and port, and the result: 0 or -errno), identity calls, clone, memfd, seccomp, perf_event_open. One stderr line per call, the first 20000 per process,
not futex/ioctl/read/write/mmap. The syscall itself runs unchanged; nothing is filtered or answered differently. Used on PGR to see what Tencent ACE reads
and which servers it reaches before it shuts down (docs/PLAN.md, CHANGELOG 2026-11-14). Module libberberis_arm64.

diff --git a/kernel_api/arm64/syscall_emulation.cc b/kernel_api/arm64/syscall_emulation.cc
--- a/kernel_api/arm64/syscall_emulation.cc
+++ b/kernel_api/arm64/syscall_emulation.cc
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
